# /onboarding is NOT here any more — it proxies to the MMS app, in netlify.toml with the
# other portal routes. Rules in this file would win over that proxy and serve the old
# static page instead, so the entry stays deleted rather than commented back in.
/onboarding-form  /onboarding  301
/welcome        /welcome.html     200

# The Test Center guide, the address the launch emails link to. Pinned, as /our-tutors is below,
# so it never depends on pretty-URL shadowing. /portal/test-center is the app; this is the page.
/test-center    /test-center.html  200

# Jobs: the admin role and the tutor role. Pinned like /test-center so the address the hiring
# emails link to never depends on pretty-URL shadowing. The tutor form itself stays at /apply.
/jobs           /jobs.html         200

# "Our Tutors" moved off /tutors, one character away from /tutor — the MMS tutor PORTAL,
# which netlify.toml proxies to Vercel. Two different audiences (a parent browsing who we
# are, versus a tutor signing in to work) separated by a single letter, and nothing on
# either page said which one you were on.
#
# Both forms 301 rather than 200: the old path is in Google's index and on whatever anyone
# has bookmarked or linked, so it has to keep resolving — but it should hand the visitor
# the new address rather than silently serve the page under a name we are retiring.
/tutors         /our-tutors  301
/tutors.html    /our-tutors  301

# Pins the bare path to the carousel so it never depends on how Netlify's splat treats a
# bare /x (netlify.toml's own comment says that's unreliable), or on pretty-URL shadowing.
/our-tutors     /our-tutors.html   200

# A single tutor's page, the link Rachit sends a parent: /our-tutors/ben-gladney.
# One static page serves every tutor; it reads the slug from the address and looks the tutor
# up in MMS's /api/public/tutors feed. Bare /our-tutors never reaches this rule — the pin above
# matches first — and tutor-profile.html redirects there itself if it ever loads with no slug.
/our-tutors/*   /tutor-profile.html   200
